	(text "ADV7513 supplies:\n  DVDD = 1.8V (digital core, generated locally by U_REG3)\n  AVDD = 1.8V (analog PLL, same rail as DVDD)\n  PVDD = 3.3V (parallel I/O — matches FPGA bank voltage)\n  TVDD = 3.3V (TMDS driver)\n  GND  = single representative pin; PCB needs ~25 ground balls connected\n\nI2C bus (FPGA -> ADV7513 config): pulled to +3V3 via 4.7k.\nDDC bus (ADV7513 -> monitor EDID): pulled to +5V via 2.2k (HDMI spec).\nHPD: comes from monitor (sources 5V when connected). 1M pulldown for stability.\n\nTODO before fab:\n  - TMDS pair ESD: TPD12S521 dedicated chip OR per-pair TVS (recommended)\n  - Common-mode chokes on TMDS pairs (board-level EMI tuning)\n  - Move +1V8 LDO to power sheet for cleaner architecture\n  - Verify ADV7513 pin numbers vs actual BGA-100 ballout (current placeholders)\n  - CEC line currently NC; route to ADV7513 CEC pin if CEC support needed"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 320 0)
